About xml :
-----------

<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Employee>
    <ID>1001</ID>   -- node
    <Name>John Doe</Name>
    <Department>IT</Department>
    <Salary currency="USD">75000</Salary>
</Employee>

->
<?xml ...?> → XML declaration (optional but recommended)
<Employee> → Root element (every XML must have one root)
<ID>, <Name>, etc. → Elements (contain data)
currency="USD" → Attribute (metadata about an element)
In XML, everything is a node — the entire document is represented as a tree of nodes (called the DOM: Document Object Model).



✅ Rule: XML is case-sensitive, and tags must be properly nested and closed.

🧩 Why XML is Used in SAP Integration (PI/PO, CPI)
Standard format for message exchange between systems
Used in:
SOAP Web Services
IDoc to XML conversion
RFC to XML
File-based interfaces (e.g., .xml files)
Both SAP PI/PO and SAP CPI use XML as the internal message format (even if source/target is JSON, IDoc, etc.)
💡 In CPI/PI, messages are converted to XML internally for processing (unless using JSON-only flows in CPI).

